<title>FRANCE: Fire guts lawcourts in central France.</title>
<headline>Fire guts lawcourts in central France.</headline>
<dateline>LYON, France 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A blaze gutted lawcourts in Roanne in central France early on Wednesday, and investigators said they suspected arson.</p>
<p>Police said the fire at about five a.m. wrecked three office floors and the roof of the Palais de Justice, housed in an 18th century convent building in the town near Lyon.</p>
<p>Investigators said the blaze may have been started by a gang of youths.</p>
